          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em dualizing object
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            which can be regarded as being an object of two different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            which is induced by homming into that object induces dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T : A^{op} \stackrel{Hom_A(-,a)}{\to} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S: B^{op} \stackrel{Hom_B(-,a)}{\to} A
                  \\,.
          %p
            Many famous dualities are induced this way, for instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone duality
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark+duality"} Gelfand-Naimark duality
          %h2#remark_on_terminology Remark on terminology
          %p
            There are various different terms for “dualizing objects”. As recalled in
            %a{:href => "#PorstTholen91"} Porst-Tholen 91, p. 112
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Isbell speaks of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em objects keeping summer and winter homes
            %li
              %p
                Lawvere speaks of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em objects sitting in two categories
            %li
              %p
                Simmons speaks of
                = succeed "." do
                  %em schizophrenic objects
          %p
            It has been convincingly argued by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
            (blog comment
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/01/more_on_duality.html#c007089"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
            then suggested the term “ambimorphic object.” Another suggestion was “Janusian object.”
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be two categories over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U : A \to Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V : B \to Set
                  \\,.
          %p
            (Traditionally in what follows, one assumed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to be faithful, i.e., one considered
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to be categories of sets with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} extra structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+categories"} concrete categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U, V
            are representable, but we won’t require this either.)
          %p
            The situation described in the Idea section asks us to consider contravariantly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T: A \to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S: B \to A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U S: B \to Set
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V T: A \to Set
            are representable, i.e., are given by isomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi U
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(-, \mathbf{b}) \cong U S
            (with representing element
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in U S \mathbf{b}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi V
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(-, \mathbf{a}) \cong V T
            (with representing element
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in V T \mathbf{a}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta: 1_A \to S T
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon: 1_B \to T S
            denote the universal maps of the adjunction (so that if we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            in covariant form as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T: A \to B^{op}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S: B^{op} \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \dashv S
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            as unit and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            as counit).
          #sitting.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The representing data
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in U S \mathbf{b}, \psi \in V T \mathbf{a}
              induce a canonical isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∼
                      %mi V
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega: U \mathbf{a} \stackrel{\sim}{\to} V \mathbf{b}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mi η
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi a
                    %mi U
                    %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi eval
                          %mi ψ
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \mathbf{a} \stackrel{U\eta \mathbf{a}}{\to} U S T \mathbf{a} \stackrel{\sim}{\to} B(T \mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}) \to Set(V T \mathbf{a}, V \mathbf{b}) \stackrel{eval_\psi}{\to} V \mathbf{b}.
            %p
              The inverse is given by a similar composite but switching the roles of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{a}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{b}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Letting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              be an element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \mathbf{a}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(x) \in V \mathbf{b}
              is by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V g)(\psi)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: T \mathbf{a} \to \mathbf{b}
              is the unique map (by representability) such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi η
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi S
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U \eta \mathbf{a})(x) = (U S g)(\phi)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{\omega}: V \mathbf{b} \to U \mathbf{a}
              takes an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in V \mathbf{b}
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U f)(\phi)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: S \mathbf{b} \to \mathbf{a}
              is the unique map such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mi T
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V T f)(\psi) = (V \epsilon \mathbf{b})(y)
            %p
              To check these maps are inverse, one may check simply
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mover
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\omega \widebar{\omega})(y) = y
              for any
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in V \mathbf{b}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{\omega} \omega = id
              follows by symmetry. With notation as above, put
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = \widebar{\omega}(y)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = (U f)(\phi) \in U \mathbf{a}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi η
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mi T
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi U
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi S
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi b
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi U
                                  %mi S
                                  %mi T
                                  %mi f
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mi T
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ξ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi B
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi T
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi b
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U S \mathbf{b} &amp; \stackrel{U f}{\to} &amp; U \mathbf{a} &amp; \stackrel{U \eta \mathbf{a}}{\to} &amp; U S T \mathbf{a} \\
                    _\mathllap{\phi} \uparrow &amp; \searrow_\mathrlap{U \eta S \mathbf{b}} &amp; &amp; _\mathllap{U S T f} \nearrow &amp; \uparrow_\mathrlap{\cong} \\
                    1 &amp; &amp; U S T S \mathbf{b} &amp; &amp; B(T \mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}) \\
                    \&amp; _\mathllap{\xi} \searrow &amp; \uparrow_\mathrlap{\cong} &amp; \nearrow _\mathrlap{B(T f, \mathbf{b})} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; B(T S \mathbf{b}, \mathbf{b}) &amp; &amp;
                    }
            %p
              where the top and right quadrilaterals commute by naturality, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: T S \mathbf{b} \to \mathbf{b}
              is the unique arrow making the left quadrilateral commute. In fact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
              is the structure map for a
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{b}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi f
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ξ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = (T \mathbf{a} \stackrel{T f}{\to} T S \mathbf{b} \stackrel{\xi}{\to} \mathbf{b})
            %p
              is the unique arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: T \mathbf{a} \to \mathbf{b}
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi S
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mi η
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U S g)(\phi) = (U \eta \mathbf{a})(x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and evaluating at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ψ
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mi T
                        %mi f
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mi ξ
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \stackrel{\psi}{\to} V T \mathbf{a} \stackrel{V T f}{\to} V T S \mathbf{b} \stackrel{V \xi}{\to} V \mathbf{b}
            %p
              equals
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y: 1 \to V \mathbf{b}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mi T
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V T f)(\psi) = (V \epsilon \mathbf{b})(y)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi b
                    %mi V
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mi ξ
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \stackrel{y}{\to} V \mathbf{b} \stackrel{V \epsilon \mathbf{b}}{\to} V T S \mathbf{b} \stackrel{V \xi}{\to} V \mathbf{b}
            %p
              and all we need to do now is check the unit equation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \circ (\epsilon \mathbf{b}) = 1_\mathbf{b}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi η
                                %mi S
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mi T
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi U
                                %mi S
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi ξ
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mi S
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi b
                                %mo ,
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi b
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    U S \mathbf{b} &amp; \stackrel{U \eta S \mathbf{b}}{\to} &amp; U S T S \mathbf{b} &amp; \stackrel{U S \epsilon \mathbf{b}}{\to} &amp; U S \mathbf{b} \\
                    _\mathllap{\phi} \uparrow &amp; &amp; \uparrow_\mathrlap{\cong} &amp; &amp; \uparrow_\mathrlap{\cong} \\
                    1 &amp; \underset{\xi}{\to} &amp; B(T S \mathbf{b}, \mathbf{b}) &amp; \underset{B(\epsilon \mathbf{b}, \mathbf{b})}{\to} &amp; B(\mathbf{b}, \mathbf{b})
                    }
            %p where the top horizontal composite is an identity, according to a triangular equation.
          %p
            The canonical identification of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi V
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega: U \mathbf{a} = V \mathbf{b}
            means that we have an object “sitting in two categories” (Lawvere), namely an
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{a}
            on this set and a
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{b}
            on the same set, with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T: A^{op} \to B
            providing a lift of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(-, \mathbf{a}): A^{op} \to Set
            through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: B \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S: B^{op} \to A
            lifting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(-, \mathbf{b}): B^{op} \to Set
            through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: A \to Set
          %p
            Given functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: A \to Set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: B \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Adj
                    %mi rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Adj_{rep}(U, V)
            to be the category whose objects are contravariantly adjoint pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S: B \to A, T: A \to B)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V T
            are representable. Morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, T) \to (S', T')
            are pairs of natural transformations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: S \to S'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta: T \to T'
            such that the diagrams
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi η
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mo ′
                          %mi T
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi S
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi α
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi S
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi S
                                %mo ′
                                %mi β
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi β
                                %mi S
                                %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ϵ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
